ne needs the tiger, then the tiger sees the lion.\n18.If someone is cold and they see the lion, then they need the tiger.\n\nNow, the question is about the mouse being cold or not.So I need to determine if the mouse is cold based on these statements.\n\nLet me start by looking at the mouse.The mouse sees the lion (statement 4).From statement 11, if someone sees the lion, they are cold.So the mouse, seeing the lion, would be cold.That seems straightforward.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any other information that might affect this.For example, does the mouse being cold depend on anything else?Statement 16 says if someone eats the mouse and the mouse sees the lion, then they are green.The mouse is not cold, as it sees the lion.</think>.\n\nThe mouse sees the lion, which makes it cold. Therefore, the option is']]
