ent "Bob is not green" would align with that implication, making it true.\n\nI think there\'s a lot of ambiguity here because the context leaves room for doubt about Bob\'s color. So, I see every reason to consider it uncertain. It could be true or false based on the given information.\n\nSo, breaking it all apart, given the ambiguity surrounding Bob\'s color, the statement that he\'s not green is true. Therefore, the answer should be A) True.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
