t.\n\nFact 8 says that if Charlie is round and quiet, then he\'s not young.But we know Charlie is young, so if he were round and quiet, that would contradict his youth.Therefore, Charlie cannot be both round and quiet because that would make him not young, but he is young.So, either Charlie is not round or not quiet, or both.\n\nWait, but fact 15 says round things are big.So, if Charlie is round, he must be big.But from fact 14, if Charlie is big and young, then he\'s not smart.But fact 7 says Harry is smart, and from fact 11, big, blue things are quiet.So, if Charlie is big and young, he would be quiet, which would make him not smart, but we know Harry is smart.Hmm, maybe that\'s a different path.\n\nLet me try to piece this together.Charlie is young.Charlie is not white.</think>.\n\nThe statement "Charlie is not white" is true because Charlie cannot be both young and white without leading to a contradiction regarding his smartness. Therefore, the answer is:. Therefore, the option is']]
