its the squirrel, then the squirrel visits the tiger.So, if the tiger is chasing something (let\'s say the dog, since the tiger chases the dog), and that something visits the squirrel, then the squirrel visits the tiger.\n\nFrom statement 23: If something visits the dog, then the dog likes the lion.So, if the dog (which is being visited by something) likes the lion, then the dog is kind (statement 24).Wait, no, statement 24 says if something is kind and visits the dog, then the dog is kind.So, if the dog is kind, then it\'s kind.That seems a bit circular.\n\nWait, maybe I should look at the implications step by step.\n\nWe know the tiger is kind (statement 13).So, according to statement 18, if something is kind, then it chases the tiger.So, the tiger, being kind, chases the tiger.The tiger does not chase the lion, as there is no direct evidence to support this claim. Despite the lion chasing the tiger, it does not imply that the tiger reciprocates by chasing the lion. Therefore, the statement remains unverified due to insufficient information.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']] 16%|#5        | 94/600 [12:08<06:15,  1.35it/s] 16%|#5        | 95/600 [12:08<04:41,  1.80it/s]
