st be blue. But if he\'s blue, he could be any other color, including white or something else.\n\nWait, but the facts don\'t mention Charlie\'s color, so we can determine it. Therefore, we can conclude for sure whether he\'s not big or big.\n\nWait, but let me think again. If Charlie is not big, he can be blue, so he must be blue. But from fact 15, if he\'s round, he\'s not big. So if he\'s round, he\'s not big. But if he\'s round, he can be quiet because he\'s young, which would make him smart. But we don\'t know if he\'s not smart.\n\nAlternatively, if he\'s round, he\'s big. So Charlie could be not round and big, or round and not big.\n\nBut without any information about Charlie\'s color or other attributes, we can determine for sure if he\'s not big.\n\nWait, but let\'s see if there\'s any other way. From fact 13: If something is not big and white, then it\'s blue. So if Charlie is not big and white, he\'s blue. But we don\'t know if Charlie is white. If he\'s white, then fact 13 doesn\'t apply, so he could be any color.\n\nBut if Charlie is not white, then from fact 12, if he\'s not young and white, he\'s round. But Charlie is not young, so if he\'s not white, he\'s round. But if he\'s not white and round, then from fact 15, he\'s not big. So if Charlie is not white, he\'s not big.\n\nBut wait, if Charlie is not white, then from fact 12, he\'s not round. Then from fact 15, he\'s not big. So if Charlie is not white, he\'s not big. But if he\'s white, he could be big.\n\nBut the facts don\'t specify if Charlie is white or not. So Charlie could be not white and not big, or white and big.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, we can determine for sure whether Charlie is not big. So the statement "Charlie is not big" could be true or unknown, but we have enough information to say it\'s definitely true or false.\n\nWait, but the options are A) True, B) False, C) Unknown. So if we can determine for sure, the answer would be C) Unknown.\n\nBut wait, let me double-check. Is there any way to conclude that Charlie is definitely not big?\n\nIf Charlie is not big, he can be blue, so he must be blue. But if he\'s blue, he could be any other color, including white. But if he\'s not white, then he\'s round and big. If he\'s white, he could be big.\n\nBut since we know his color, we can conclude he\'s not big. Therefore, the statement "Charlie is not big" could be true if he\'s not big, but we can confirm it because he might be big if he\'s white.\n\nWait, but if Charlie is white, he\'s not big. So if he\'s white, he\'s not big, making the statement false. If he\'s not white, he\'s big, making the statement true. But since we know, the statement could be either true or unknown.\n\nWait, but the question is asking if the statement is true, false, or unknown. So if there\'s any possibility that the statement is true, and any possibility that it\'s false, then it\'s unknown.\n\nBut in this case, the statement is "Charlie is not big." If Charlie is not big, the statement is false. If he\'s big, the statement is true. Since we know, the answer is C) Unknown.\n\nWait, but let me think again. Maybe there\'s a way to conclude that Charlie is not big. Let\'s see.\n\nFrom fact 14: If Charlie is not big and young, then he\'s smart. But we don\'t know if he\'s not smart. So if he\'s not big and young, he\'s not smart. But if he\'s big, we know.\n\nFrom fact 15: Not round things are not big. So if Charlie is not round, he\'s not big. But if he\'s not round, from fact 8, he can be quiet because he\'s young. But if he\'s not big and not blue, he has to be quiet.\n\nBut if Charlie is round, he\'s big. So Charlie could be not round and not big, or round and big.\n\nBut without knowing if he\'s round or not, we can determine.\n\nWait, but let\'s see if Charlie is not white. If he\'s not white, then from fact 12, he\'s not round, which makes him not big. So if he\'s not white, he\'s not big. If he\'s white, he could be big.\n\nBut since we know, the