owever, the question is only about whether Gary is not big, not his color.\n\nSo, based on point 16, since Gary is not rough, he must not be big.There\'s no information that contradicts this.Even though we don\'t know if Gary is not green, that doesn\'t affect his size.So the statement "Gary is not big" should be true.\n\nI don\'t see any other rules that would make this false.The only thing we\'re unsure about is Gary\'s color, but that\'s irrelevant to the question about his size.\n\nSo, the answer should be B) False.\n\n</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
