is big and green, he must be furry.But from point 11, all furry people are white.So if Gary is furry, he must be white.\n\nWait, but let me double-check.Point 11 says all furry people are white, so if Gary is furry, he\'s white.But Gary is green, which is a different color.So does being green affect this?No, because the color is green, but the fur\'s color is white.So Gary\'s fur is white, making him white overall.\n\nSo putting it all together: Gary is green, quiet, smart, big, and therefore must be furry and white.So the statement "Gary is white" should be false.\n\n</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
