round, then it needs the cat.\n17.If something visits the squirrel, then the squirrel visits the dog.\n18.If something is nice, then it sees the dog.\n19.If something needs the cat, then it is nice.\nThe bald eagle does not need the squirrel, as statement 4 clearly states "The bald eagle does not need the squirrel." This contradicts the given information, making the statement false. Therefore, the answer should be B) False.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
