perties.\n\nDisregarding the rules:\n\n- No smart, round people are blue.So, if someone is not smart or round, they cannot be blue.Dave is blue, but we don\'t know if he\'s smart or round.However, the question is about him being red, which he isn\'t, so that doesn\'t affect the answer.\n\n- If someone is red, then they are not young (rule 13).Since Dave is blue, this rule doesn\'t apply to him.\n\n- If Fiona is not round, she\'s red (rule 12).But Fiona is round, so she\'s red, but that doesn\'t affect Dave.\n\n- Harry is red and round, but the rules about Harry not being young and round leading to him not being rough don\'t affect Dave.\n\n- White people are not smart (rule 16), but Dave is blue, so that\'s irrelevant.\n\n- Young people are not round (rule 17).Again, Dave\'s color is blue, so his age isn\'t specified, but the rule doesn\'t change his color.\n\nSo, all the rules and facts point to Dave being blue, not red.Therefore, the statement "Dave is red" is false.\n\n</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
