 kind yet.So we can\'t directly say if she\'s young or not based on that.\n\nFact 16 says all big things are round.Since Fiona is big, she must be round.\n\nFact 17 says if something is round, then it is kind.So since Fiona is round (from fact 16), she must be kind.Therefore, Fiona is kind.\n\nBut the question is asking if Fiona is not kind.Since we\'ve just concluded Fiona is kind, the statement "Fiona is not kind" would be true.\n\nWait, let me double-check.Maybe I missed something.Let\'s go through it again.\n\nFiona is big (fact 12).All big things are round (fact 16), so Fiona is round.If something is round, it\'s kind (fact 17), so Fiona is kind.Therefore, Fiona is kind, so the statement "Fiona is not kind" is true.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions or missing information here.So the answer should be that the statement is true.\n\n</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
