 statement 9 says nice, big things are white.So, if Gary is nice and big, he must be white.But he\'s red, so that\'s a contradiction.\n\nWait, that can\'t be right.Maybe I\'m missing something.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps Gary is not big.Let me see.If Gary is young, and from statement 14, all quiet things are big, and Gary is quiet, then Gary must be big.But from statement 15, he\'s red.So, he\'s big and red.From statement 12, big, red things are young, which he is.So, that\'s consistent.\n\nBut then, from statement 9, nice, big things are white.So, if Gary is nice and big, he must be white.Gary is not big, so the statement "Gary is big" is true.</think>.\n\nThe statement "Gary is big" is false because if Gary were big, he would have to be both white and red, which is impossible. Therefore, Gary cannot be big. Therefore, the option is']] 48%|####8     | 291/600 [16:24<01:01,  5.02it/s] 49%|####8     | 292/600 [16:24<00:54,  5.68it/s]
