ince Fiona is nice, she must be round (fact 5 and 12).\n\nThen, from fact 16, round things are blue.So Fiona, being round, is blue.Now, from fact 8, all blue things are white.So Fiona is blue and therefore white, which we already knew from fact 6.\n\nNow, let\'s see if being blue affects anything else.Fact 14 says all blue things are young.So Fiona, being blue, is young.Which we already knew from fact 7.\n\nBut wait, fact 10 says all young, blue things are not green.Since Fiona is blue and young, she\'s not green.That\'s consistent, but doesn\'t affect her being cold.\nBased on the information provided, it is unclear whether Fiona is not cold.</think>.\n\nThe statement "Fiona is not cold" is unknown because there is no information linking Fiona\'s color or state to coldness. All facts about Fiona concern her being nice, white, and young, but not her coldness. Therefore, the option is']]
