messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is quiet. Bob is not rough. Gary is big. Gary is kind. Gary is rough. Gary is young. Harry is young. All big people are furry. Young people are furry. All quiet, kind people are furry. If Harry is furry and Harry is quiet then Harry is round. Rough, kind people are quiet. Young, rough people are kind. All quiet, furry people are round. Furry people are rough.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is young.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Gary is young" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:\n\n1.Anne is quiet.\n2.Bob is not rough.\n3.Gary is big.\n4.Gary is kind.\n5.Gary is rough.\n6.Gary is young.\n7.Harry is young.\n8.All big people are furry.\n9.Young people are furry.\n10.All quiet, kind people are furry.\n11.If Harry is furry and Harry is quiet, then Harry is round.\n12.Rough, kind people are quiet.\n13.Young, rough people are kind.\n14.All quiet, furry people are round.\n15.Furry people are rough.\n\nWait, that\'s a lot.Let me see if I can organize this better.\n\nLooking at point 6 and 5: Gary is both big and rough.But point 3 says Gary is big, and point 5 says Gary is rough.However, point 6 also says Gary is young.So, according to the given information, Gary is young.\n\nBut let me check if there\'s any contradiction or if I\'m missing something.Let\'s go through each point again.\nGary is not young, rough, or big.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
