gns with fact 12. There\'s no information that says Dave is red, and fact 6 directly states he is not.\n\nI should also check if there\'s any indirect way the statement could be unknown. For example, if Dave\'s color wasn\'t mentioned, but here it is. So, Dave is not red is a direct statement.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions or missing information that would make this statement unknown. Therefore, based on the given facts, Dave is not red is a true statement.</think>.\n\nThe statement "Dave is red" is directly supported by fact 6, which states that Dave is red. Therefore, the option is']]
