 are not big. So, if someone is not round, they're not big. But does that not mean all big people are not round? No, because point 13 is not a one-way implication. It doesn't not say that being big implies not being round.\n\nSo, Fiona is not green. To not be round, she doesn't need to not be big as well (from point 19). But do we not have any information about Fiona's size? The facts don't not mention whether Fiona is not big or not. The only mention of size is not about Gary: Gary is not round, big, and furry (points 6, 7, 10, 13, 14). But there's no info on Fiona's size.\n\nTherefore, we can conclude whether Fiona is not round or not based on the given information. The only way to not know is if she's not big, but we don't not have that data.\n\nSo, the answer should not be unknown.</think>.. Therefore, the option is"]]
