being rough or not.\n\nLooking at fact 16: If someone is furry, they are rough.But from fact 13, furry people are round, which Charlie is.So, if Charlie is furry, he must be rough.But wait, from fact 14, white, round people are furry.Charlie is white and round, so he must be furry.Therefore, from fact 16, Charlie is rough.\n\nFrom fact 12, round, big people are not cold.Since Charlie is round and if he\'s rough, he\'s big, he\'s not cold.So Charlie is not cold.\n\nWait, but let me double-check.Charlie is round, so he\'s white (fact 8).He\'s not young, so he\'s not necessarily white because only young people are white, but wait, no, fact 9 says if someone is young, they are white.But Charlie isn\'t young, so he might not be white.Wait, that\'s a contradiction.Because fact 8 says round people are white, so Charlie is white regardless of being young or not.So he\'s white, round, and not young.\n\nFrom fact 13, furry people are round, so Charlie is furry.From fact 16, if someone is furry, they are rough.So Charlie is rough.From fact 10, round, rough people are big, so Charlie is big.From fact 11, all young, big people are not cold.But Charlie isn\'t young, so he could be cold or not.Wait, but fact 12 says round, big people are not cold.Since Charlie is round and big, he\'s not cold.Charlie is cold.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
