ne sees the rabbit and the rabbit is green, then they are young.\n15.If someone likes the squirrel and they are red, then they are young.\n16.If someone sees the squirrel and the squirrel sees the mouse, then they like the rabbit.\n\nNow, the question is about whether the mouse does not see the mouse.So, I need to determine if the mouse sees itself or not.\n\nLooking at the statements, I don\'t see any direct information about the mouse seeing itself.Let\'s see if any of the other statements can lead us to that conclusion.Based on the information provided, it is evident that the mouse does not see itself or any other condition that would suggest otherwise.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
