t, no, fact 2 says Bob is quiet, but nothing about Gary.So we don\'t know if Gary is quiet or not.\n\nFact 11: If someone is smart and white, then they are green.But Gary is red, so even if he were smart and white, he would have to be green.But we don\'t know if Gary is smart or white.\n\nFact 8: If someone is smart and big, then they are white.Gary is big, but we don\'t know if he\'s smart.If he were smart, then he would have to be white.But Gary is red, so if he were smart and big, he\'d be white, but he\'s red, so that creates a contradiction.Therefore, Gary cannot be smart because if he were, he\'d have to be both white and red, which isn\'t possible.So Gary is not smart.\nGary is not green based on the given facts.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
