nsistent because Bob is not big or round.\n\nPoint 15 says if Bob is not red, then he\'s big.But Bob is red (point 7), so this affects him.Point 17 says red people are not kind, so Bob is not kind.Point 20 says kind people are not big, which contradicts Bob being big.\n\nPoint 14: If someone is big and round, they are not green.Bob is big and round, so he shouldn\'t be green, which he isn\'t (point 6).So that\'s contradictory.\n\nPoint 13: All blue people are round.Since Bob is red, this applies to him.\n\nPoint 18: If Gary is blue, then Gary is not furry.But Gary is furry (point 11), so Gary must not be blue.But that\'s not directly related to Bob.\n\nPoint 19: If someone is kind and green, they are not furry.Bob is kind and green, so he shouldn\'t be furry, which he isn\'t (point 5).So that\'s contradictory.\n\nEverything seems to be inconsistent with many contradictions.Therefore, the statement "Bob is round" is definitely false based on the given information.\n\n</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
