g green and smart, but that\'s only for Gary.But Fiona is round, but we don\'t know her color or other traits.\n\nWait, let\'s see fact 17: If Harry is blue and Harry is smart, then Harry is quiet.But Harry is smart (fact 10), but we don\'t know if he\'s blue.From fact 13, if Harry is blue, he\'s green.But he\'s smart, and from fact 16, smart people are green.So if Harry is blue, he\'s green and smart, which fits.But we don\'t know if he\'s blue or not.So Harry could be blue, making him quiet, but that\'s not directly related to Fiona.\n\nSo, going back to Fiona.She\'s round.Let\'s see if being round implies anything else.From fact 15: Nice, round people are blue.So if someone is nice and round, they are blue.But Fiona is only round.So unless she\'s nice, we can\'t say she\'s blue.But if she\'s nice and round, she\'s blue, which would make her green and smart.But we don\'t know if she\'s nice.\n\nAlternatively, if she\'s not nice, then she\'s not nice and round, so she\'s not blue.But that doesn\'t tell us anything about her being smart or not.\n\nFiona is not smart.</think>.. Therefore, the option is']]
